# Oblivion from New Game: the game selector hands off to Charactergen stage 5 (CharGenQuest then starts MQ01, the
# tutorial, and moves the player into the Imperial Prison cell) and pops the RaceSex Menu. The player confirms the race
# menu; the prisoners talk (Valen Dreth, then Renote/Glenroy/Baurus), Glenroy opens the cell door and the Emperor greets
# the player. Everything between is NPC-driven: the cases only WAIT for it.
# Stages used are Charactergen's (TES4 numbers): 5 start, 6 Valen Dreth, 9 Valen done, 10-13 Renote/Glenroy talk,
# 14 player in the trigger zone, 15 door open, 16 Emperor at marker B, 17 Emperor force-greets, 18 Renote to the switch,
# 19 secret wall open.

case chargen_start
until 900 GetStage Charactergen >= 5
expect GetQuestRunning MQ01
end

# Menu expected: "RaceSex Menu" (TESGameSelect BeginChosenGame calls Game.ShowRaceMenu 0.5 s after the hand-off).
# God mode stands in for the player being strong enough for the later fights (it is not a story change).
case chargen_race_menu
wait 60
close RaceSex Menu
console tgm
end

# MQ01 stage 5 enables controls and sets its own stage 10 two seconds later; stage 10 sets Charactergen 6.
case chargen_tutorial_starts
until 600 GetStageDone MQ01 10
until 300 GetStage Charactergen >= 6
end

# Valen Dreth taunts from the next cell (CharGenTaunt2 conversation INFO sets stage 9), then the Emperor's group
# conversation chain runs on the speaker/target handshake (INFO 00032B04 sets stage 10).
case chargen_prisoners_talk
until 3600 GetStage Charactergen >= 9
until 3600 GetStage Charactergen >= 10
end

# Renote reaches marker A outside the cell (stage 12); Renote/Glenroy finish talking about the player (INFO 00032B0E sets 13).
case chargen_renote_at_marker_a
until 3600 GetStage Charactergen >= 12
until 3600 GetStage Charactergen >= 13
end

# Stage 13 waits for the player to be inside the CGTriggerZoneCell trigger box, away from the cell door. The player
# walks into the middle of the cell; moveto stands in for the walk. The ref has no EditorID in Oblivion.esm, so the
# TES4 FormID of the placed trigger (00097A3B, Imperial Prison cell) is used.
case chargen_step_into_cell
run
player.moveto 00097A3B
until 600 GetStage Charactergen >= 14
end

# Glenroy opens the cell door (15) and the Emperor walks to marker B and speaks to the player (16); the quest script
# then sets 17 and the Emperor force-greets with "Let me see your face...".
case chargen_cell_door_opens
until 1800 GetStage Charactergen >= 15
until 1800 GetStage Charactergen >= 16
until 1800 GetStage Charactergen >= 17
hear 1800 UrielSeptimRef Let me see your face
end

# The Emperor's force-greet opens the dialogue menu on its own (no talk). The player asks the three questions that set
# Charactergen.what / .who / .why, then "What should I do?" (only offered once all three are 1) which hands the
# conversation to Renote.
case chargen_emperor_in_cell
wait 30
ask "What's going on?"
ask "Who are you?"
ask "Why am I in jail?"
expect Charactergen.what == 1
expect Charactergen.who == 1
expect Charactergen.why == 1
ask "What should I do?"
bye
end

# Renote crosses to the secret-wall switch (stage 18, set by INFO 0004D84C when the Renote/Emperor exchange ends);
# she activates it (CGPrisonSecretWallSwitchSCRIPT sets secretDoor), and CharGenQuest sets 19 once the wall has opened.
case chargen_secret_wall
until 3600 GetStage Charactergen >= 18
until 3600 GetStage Charactergen >= 19
expect Charactergen.secretDoor == 1
end
